content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Client",
      "description": "Person or group requesting a concert event."
    },
    {
      "name": "Client Request",
      "description": "Initial request outlining what the client wants."
    },
    {
      "name": "Event Manager",
      "description": "Coordinator responsible for planning the concert event."
    },
    {
      "name": "Concert Event Proposal",
      "description": "Draft proposal describing the event concept and scope."
    },
    {
      "name": "Revision Request",
      "description": "Client’s request for changes to the proposal."
    },
    {
      "name": "Event Plan",
      "description": "Detailed plan for executing the concert."
    },
    {
      "name": "Progress Update",
      "description": "Status message reporting planning progress."
    },
    {
      "name": "Venue Request",
      "description": "Request sent to a venue for booking details.",
      "attributes": [
        "Concert Date",
        "Venue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Concert Date",
      "description": "Specific date proposed for the event."
    },
    {
      "name": "Venue",
      "description": "Location where the concert may take place."
    },
    {
      "name": "Venue Manager",
      "description": "Manager responsible for venue availability and resources."
    },
    {
      "name": "Technical Crew Member",
      "description": "Crew member responsible for technical setup."
    },
    {
      "name": "Equipment Check",
      "description": "Verification of technical equipment readiness."
    },
    {
      "name": "Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Person responsible for promoting the concert."
    },
    {
      "name": "Promotional Material",
      "description": "Marketing assets created for the event."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ticket Campaign",
      "description": "Plan for ticket sales and distribution.",
      "attributes": [
        "Sales Data",
        "Ticket"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sales Data",
      "description": "Information on ticket sales performance."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ticket",
      "description": "Ticket made available for purchase.",
      "attributes": [
        "Category",
        "Price"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Category",
      "description": "Ticket class or seating type."
    },
    {
      "name": "Price",
      "description": "Cost assigned to a ticket."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ticketing Manager",
      "description": "Person overseeing ticket sales and distribution."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ticket Sale Report",
      "description": "Summary report of ticket sales."
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Event Supervision": {
      "objects": [
        "Event Manager",
        "Event Plan"
      ]
    },
    "Sales": {
      "objects": [
        "Marketing Coordinator",
        "Promotional Material",
        "Ticket Campaign",
        "Sales Data",
        "Ticket",
        "Price",
        "Category",
        "Ticketing Manager",
        "Ticket Sale Report"
      ]
    },
    "Venue Organisation": {
      "objects": [
        "Venue Request",
        "Concert Date",
        "Venue",
        "Venue Manager",
        "Technical Crew Member",
        "Equipment Check"
      ]
    },
    "Client Interaction": {
      "objects": [
        "Client",
        "Client Request",
        "Event Manager",
        "Concert Event Proposal",
        "Revision Request",
        "Progress Update"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
